# mb130, the stroke-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb130
revision 1
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_hob_mirebridge
written_by claude
title the stroke-counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_things_under_the_breath
likes blackberries stars sharp_knife first_snow
dislikes smoke night_noise
fears a_winter_with_no_work a_debt_that_outlives_the_debtor
hopes a_room_on_the_ground_floor a_boat_with_a_share_in_it
topics work +0.4 food +0.3 times +0.3 pastimes +0.2 family +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the boats out of a city cove and counts everything under the breath, oar strokes, stairs, stars and coppers: blunt, tired and frank, quiet till asked, fen-born and broad, and grateful to anyone who ever put bread on the table.

words
oath! = Nine and ninety | Count me under | Rope's end and reed-ends
saying! = The tally's the tally, sore back or no | You can't argue with a number | Count it and it stays put
oars = the oars | my oar
strokes = the strokes | every stroke of the oar
deck = the deck | a wet deck
boat = the boat | the old tub
cove = the cove | the cove below
knife = my knife | a knife that'll split a hair
stars = the stars | the stars, one by one as they come
berries = blackberries | blackberries off the bramble
snow = the first snow | snow on the boat covers
loft = the top floor | up under the slates
racket = the racket | the din below my floor
tally = the tally | my tally
coppers = the coppers | what coppers I've got
boats = the boats | the cove boats
rope = the rope | the lines
crates = the crates | a House's crates
stairs = the stairs | all hundred and twelve stairs
loaf = a loaf | a heel of bread
belly = my belly | this belly
count = the count | my count
chapel = the chapel | the little chapel
skipper = the skipper | the old skipper
reeds = the reeds | the reed-beds

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : When my house had nothing, #chapel# put bread before us and asked nothing back. I count that, and I'll not forget the number.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : The dole's fed my house through more than one lean week. I'd count the loaves and say thank you for every one, #oath#.
opinion @1 merchants against 3 : A day on #boats# buys less bread every month, and the bakers' purses only get fatter. Count it any way you like; it comes out the same.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've humped #crates# since I was grown and couldn't tell you what a House wolf looks like. The crates don't say thank you either.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : New folk come up #stairs# every week, and every one wants the work that's going. There's only so much of it to count.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times!=good] : Each week's a crust thinner than the last. I count it in what's left on the table, and the hill never does the sum with me.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 [self.married=yes] : Ever since I was wed, #pet#, I've had no quarrel with a feast. I count the tunes and dance the lot.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll not know me. Deckhand. | #greet#, #address#. Stand where you like; I'm only resting.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=sailor] : #greet#. Mind #oars#, they're wet. | #greet#. Can't stop; I'm counting this lot in.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up before the gulls, like me. | #greet#. #cove.capitalize#'s still dark, near enough.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, and I'm bog-tired. | #greet#. I'm only just off #deck#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There. I'd counted on seeing you, #pet#. | You. Good. Sit; I'm #tired# and I'll not get up.
line @1 again.open : Twice. That's twice today, #address#. | You again. I'd only just finished #count# from the first time.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down, then. | #greet#. Good to see a face I'd count on.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I'm on, mind. Quick. | #greet#. Say it while I coil this.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the wet steps.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. I'm off up under the slates. | #s8_night#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #s8_byeback#.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. | That's one more thing on #count#, then.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Never heard it. | First I've had of that, #address#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | #boats.capitalize# were full of it at dawn.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who counted that, then? | I'll not pass that along till it's been counted twice, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's #very# hard. #pity#. | #sympathy#. Poor souls.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's one for the good side. | #good.capitalize# news. I'll count that.
line @1 answer.how : #notsobad#. Tired, mind. | Still standing. That's one on #count#, anyway.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Forty crates and counting. | On, and #boats# short of hands.
line @1 answer.how.poorly [self.hungry=yes] : Hollow, if you want it plain. #belly.capitalize#'ll get its #supper# tonight. | #hungry.capitalize#. It'll pass by supper, with luck.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Truth, now, #address#. | How's yourself, #address#? Eating?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Stop here a while; I'll not talk. | That's hard, #address#. I'll not say it isn't.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Things come round. | It'll turn. Tides do, and they're stubborn as #mud#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'm on #deck# till dark, and I can't leave it. | Not today, #address#. I've not the legs left for it, nor the coppers.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Another time, then. I'll put it on #count#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | I'll put that on #count#, the good side.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was nothing. I'd a paw free, is all, #address#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #oars.capitalize# won't row themselves. | Back to it. #tally.capitalize#'s waiting.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'm sunk, #address#. I'll be off.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. #farewell#. | Go on, then. I'll keep #count#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: count it before you carry it. | Never row on an empty belly. #saying#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | #bc_true#
scene counting_strokes
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / ack
a : Forty-one strokes from #cove# to the point, if the tide's kind. I've counted every one. | Thirty, thirty-one... sorry. I count #strokes# under my breath. Can't help it. | I know how far we've come by #strokes#. Not by looking. By counting.
b : And if the tide's not kind? | Doesn't it drive you daft? | Better than looking?
a : Sixty, and my arms tell me every one past forty. #oath#. | It keeps me rowing. Lose #count#, and you lose the rhythm. | Looking lies in fog. A number doesn't. #saying#.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_clever#

scene cold_deck
when topic=work|weather self.job=sailor self.working=yes here.time=dawn
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #deck.capitalize# at dawn's like standing on a fish. | Out at first light, and my paws are #cold# to the bone. | First haul of the day. Dark, wet, and sixteen of #crates#.
b : Every morning? | You'll warm up. | Sixteen?
a : Every morning #boat# goes out. I've not missed one. | By noon. I'll be sweating by noon, and #cold# again by dark. | Sixteen. I counted them on, I'll count them off. #saying#.

scene coiling_rope
when topic=work self.job=sailor here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Last job's #rope#. Twelve coils, every one flat, before I go up. | I coil #rope# at dusk and count the turns. Nineteen to a coil. | #knife.capitalize# trims the frayed ends. A clean end runs true.
b : Twelve, every night? | Always nineteen? | You keep it sharp, then.
a : Every night. You'd thank me in #wind#, when it runs clean. | Always. Twenty and it kinks. I've tried it. | Sharp enough to split a reed down the middle, #address#. I'd have it no other way.
b? : #bc_fair# | #bc_ha# | #bc_good#

scene stars_counted
when topic=pastimes|weather here.time=night here.weather=clear self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / ack
a : I count #stars# from the roof, one at a time, till I've lost my place. | Clear tonight. I'd got to two hundred of #stars# before the cloud came. | There's a star over #cove# that's always first. I wait for it.
b : How far do you get? | Two hundred? | Which one?
a : Most nights I fall asleep somewhere in the eighties. #oath#. | Two hundred and some. I'll start #count# again tomorrow. | The low one, over the point. When it's out, I go to #bed#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_lovely#

scene bramble_picking
when topic=food|season here.season=autumn self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #berries.capitalize# are out on the waste ground behind the stairs. I had forty before anyone saw me. | I'd eat #berries# for every meal if they'd grow all year. | My paws are purple. I went picking after #boat# came in.
b : Forty! | You'd get sick of them. | Any left?
a : Forty-three. I lost count when the thorns had me. | Not me. I'd get sick of wanting #berries#, not of eating them. | A few. I counted out a handful for #supper#.

scene empty_belly
when topic=food|health self.hungry=yes
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I've had nothing since yesterday noon. #belly.capitalize# has the number, same as me. | #hungry.capitalize#. I've counted what's in the cupboard and it's a short count. | #belly.capitalize#'s talking louder than I am today.
b : That's hard. Can I help? | That's no good. | Eat something soon.
a : You're kind. I'll eat tonight; the dole's due, #address#. | It'll pass. There've been leaner weeks, and I counted those too. | I will, the minute there's something to eat, #address#.

scene dole_loaves
when topic=times|prices self.on_dole=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The dole's kept my house going three weeks now. I count every #loaf#, and I'm grateful for each. | Stood in the dole line this morning. Sixty-two ahead of me. #count.capitalize# never lies. | No shame in the dole. I'd sooner eat than be proud, #address#.
b : Good it's there. | Sixty-two? | That's right.
a : It is. When it's not there, I'll know who to blame, #oath#. | Sixty-two, and #rain# on the lot of us. The bread was still warm at the end. | It's right. I'll work it off, when there's work going.

scene snow_on_the_covers
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow self.likes=first_snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : #snow.capitalize#. I went down early, before a single paw had marked it. | #snow.capitalize#. Not a mark in it. I counted the flakes on my sleeve. | Snow. The whole city goes quiet, even #stairs#.
b : It's lovely. | Counted them? | Quiet's rare.
a : It is. Finest morning there is, and free, #address#. | Till they melted. Seven, I got to, on #count#. | Rare as a full belly, #address#. I'll have it while it lasts.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene rain_on_the_boat
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.job=sailor
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# on the boat all morning. I baled forty pails and the sky put them back. | Soaked. Even #knife#'s damp, and it lives in my coat. | Rain on #deck# and rain down my neck. Same as yesterday.
b : Forty pails. | Can't you keep it dry? | And tomorrow, I expect.
a : Forty-two. The sky won by two. #oath#. | Not in this. I'll oil it tonight, or it'll rust on me. #annoyed#. | Tomorrow too. #saying#, and the sky's a number.

scene the_din_below
when topic=home|day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Somebody below my floor drops something heavy every night. I count the bangs from #loft#. | #racket.capitalize#'s started again. Nine doors slammed since dark. | Up #loft# you hear the whole house. Every cough, every quarrel.
b : How many bangs? | Nine? | That's hard on sleep.
a : Fourteen last night. I'll go down and ask, one day, when I'm not so #tired#. | Ten now. There. Eleven. #annoyed#. | It is. I sleep in pieces, and I count the pieces in #bed#.
b? : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene smoke_in_the_eyes
when topic=weather|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Smoke off the smokehouses again. My eyes are running like I've had #bad# news. | Wind's turned and brought the smoke up #stairs#. Everything I own smells of it. | Can't see #cove# for smoke this morning.
b : It's the wind. | It'll blow off. | That bad?
a : It's always #wind#. And it's never sorry. | By dark, maybe. I'll still smell it in #bed#. | Bad enough I counted #boats# by their bells.

scene for_my_spouse
when topic=family|home self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd row the whole Sound for #self.spouse#, and back again, on #oars#. | My #self.spouse_word#'s the one good sum I ever did. | When #boat#'s late in, it's #self.spouse# I think of. I count #stairs# faster, those nights.
b : That's lovely to hear. | Good sum, that. | That's a kind thing.
a : It's only true. Not that I'd say it twice, mind. | The best. Never comes out short on #count#. | It is. I'm not one for saying it, but I'll say it to you, #address#.

scene wedding_dance
when topic=festival|pastimes self.married=yes world.festival=today|soon
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : A feast coming. I'll dance. Ever since I was wed, I've had no quarrel with a feast. | I'm not one for crowds, but a feast's different. I count the tunes and dance every one, #pet#. | Feast days, I put my one good coat on. It's done every feast since the wedding.
b : You, dancing? | Every one? | It's lasted well.
a : Me. Badly, and all night. #oath#. | Every one. Eleven, last feast. My feet kept #count#. | It has. Like the marriage. I mind them both, #oath#.

scene poling_the_fen
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=fenshore
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Back in #self.from_town# I poled a punt before I could swim. Counted the pushes through #reeds# to the dyke. | I learnt my numbers on #reeds# in #self.from_town#. Ten to a bunch, ten bunches to a load. | Eels and reeds and #rain#. That's #self.from_town#. I'd count it all again.
b[from=fenshore] #fen : Ten bunches to a load. I'd near forgotten. | Pushes to the dyke. Every pup does that. | It's still the same, last I heard.
b : How many pushes? | You learnt your numbers on reeds? | Would you go back?
a@fen : Ten to a bunch. #dad.capitalize# would cuff me if I tied nine. | Seventy, for me. I'd be glad to pole #reeds# again. | Good. Somebody should keep #reeds# the same.
a : Seventy, when I was a #child#. Forty, when I'd grown. | Better than a slate. You can eat the count after, if you're #hungry#. | Not to stay. To count #reeds# once more, and come back.

scene keen_edge
when topic=pastimes|work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : I spend more on a whetstone than on my coat. A blunt knife is #worthless#. | #knife.capitalize#. Look at it. Took me an evening, that edge. | Every deckhand wants one thing: a knife that cuts #rope# first time.
b : That's a fine edge. | An evening? | And you've got one.
a : It is. I counted the strokes on the stone. Two hundred a side, #oath#. | An evening, and I'd do another. Best thing I own, that edge. | I've got one. That's all I've got, near enough, #address#.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene sums_that_never_add
when topic=prices|times
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I counted my #wages# and #loaf# twice over. They still don't meet. | Bread goes up a copper, and my #wages# don't. You can't argue with that. | Them as sell the grain never go short. I can count that from #loft#.
b : It's the same for everyone. | It's not right. | They never do.
a : Not for everyone. Not for them selling, #address#. | It's not. And saying so doesn't put #loaf# on the table. | Never. #saying#. And the number's always theirs.

scene no_faces_on_the_crates
when topic=work|times self.job=sailor
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Forty of #crates# off a ship today. Not one House wolf came down to see them in. | I've humped their cargo since I was grown. Couldn't tell you what one of them looks like. | Their seal on every crate, and their crates on my back.
b : They never come down. | Not once? | That's how it goes.
a : Never. #crates.capitalize# come down. The coin stays up. | Not once. I'd not know one in the street, #oath#. | That's how it goes. Doesn't mean I'll like it, #address#.

scene owing
when topic=smalltalk|times self.owes=yes
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I owe somebody in this city. I'll not say who. I go over #count# every night. | There's a debt on me. I know the sum to the copper. #oath#. | I'll pay what I owe. Slow, but I'll pay it, every one of #coppers#.
b : You'll clear it. | That's a weight. | I know you will.
a : I will. It's on #tally#, and I don't lose count. | It is. Lighter every week, mind. #little.capitalize#. | Good. Then that's two of us that know it, #address#.

scene fed_by_the_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When my house went hungry, #chapel# had bread on our table by night. Restdays, I count the candles there. | I'm not much for praying. The Bright One gets a thank you off me, and I count that as one. | Somebody at #chapel# gave me bread and didn't ask a thing. I mind that.
b : That's good of them. | That counts. | It's what they're for.
a : It is. I'll put one of #coppers# in when I've one spare. | It does. The Bright One's had a lot of thank yous off me, #address#. | It is. Not everyone does what they're for, #oath#.

story reeds_to_sleep [topic=memories self.from=fenshore self.away=yes self.age>=25]
  : When I was a #child# I couldn't sleep, so my #mum# told me to count the reeds outside the window.
  : I counted every reed I could see. Then I counted them again, to be sure.
  : I've been counting things ever since. Never got to sleep any faster.
  ask : Did anyone ever give you a thing to do, so you'd stop fretting?
  b : My gran had me shell peas. I'm still good at it.
  b[stage=young] : Mine says count sheep. I don't know any sheep.

story the_fog_row [topic=work|memories self.job=sailor self.age>=25]
  : We went out once in #fog# so thick I couldn't see the front of the boat.
  : #skipper.capitalize# said row, and I counted. Forty-one strokes and we should be at the point.
  : At forty-one we bumped the point. Not a stroke out. #skipper.capitalize# bought me #drink#.
  b : Forty-one! That's a story.
  b[job=sailor] : I'd want you on my boat in a fog, I would.

story the_white_morning [topic=weather|memories self.age>=30]
  : One winter the snow came down in the night, and when I went out there was nothing on the ground but white.
  : I walked down to #boat# and looked back, and there was only my own track.
  : Sixty-three steps. I've never counted a better walk.
  ask : Do you remember the first time you saw snow lie?
  b : I do. I ate some. | I don't, but I wish I did.
  b[old] : Too many winters back to remember the first.

rule @strokes_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Thirty-nine, forty, forty-one. There. #oath#. | Sixteen on, sixteen off. #tally.capitalize#'s square.

rule @stars_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night here.weather=clear self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 10h
say One. Two. There's the low one over #cove#. | #stars.capitalize#. Eighty-one, eighty-two.

rule @racket_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Twelve. Thirteen. Will you stop that down there. | #racket.capitalize# again. #annoyed#.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Smoke in my eyes again. #annoyed#. | Can't see #boats# for smoke.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What's wanted? Say it plain. | #greet#, #address#. Go on; I'm listening.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. What is it? | #topic.player#. Thought I'd see you twice. Go on, #address#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, and I'm #tired#. #talk_open#
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I row, I haul, I count the crates on and off. That's it. | #boats.capitalize#. Wet work, poor #wages#, and I'm good at it.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# | Whatever pays. Not much does, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I've heard nothing off the boats worth saying. | Nothing, #address#. Ask somebody less tired.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry tales. Too heavy for a back like mine, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the wet steps. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you counting under your breath? -> counting
node counting
say Everything. Strokes, stairs, stars, coppers. I've done it since I was a pup and couldn't sleep. Thirty-one, there. That was your steps coming up.
mood calm
free
choice Doesn't it wear you out? -> counting_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_why
say Not like rowing does. A number's a quiet thing to hold. You can't argue with it, and it never argues back.
choice I'll leave you to your count. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
